 "read_me": {
  "Doors/deal": "How many homes you have to work to find one deal. A smaller number is better.",
  "Vs baseline": "How many times better this list is than mailing every home in the county. 5x means five times better.",
  "Deals (6mo)": "How many homes from this list an investor bought in the last 6 months.",
  "Deal Share %": "Out of all the deals in this county, how many came from this list.",
  "List Size": "How many homes are on this list right now.",
  "Typical gross": "The profit built into a typical deal here: what the home is worth minus what it sold for.",
  "Priority": "Work the Priority 1 rows first. They find deals the fastest. Then Priority 2. Priority 3 is extra.",
  "Signal": "The list of homes this row is about.",
  "Type": "List = homes on one list. Stack = homes on two lists at once. AI score = homes the computer score picked.",
  "Rung": "The order to pull in. Rung 1 is the best value in the county, then work down.",
  "New deals reached": "Deals this rung unlocks that the rungs above it did not already cover.",
  "Market share after %": "Out of all this county's investor deals, the share your stack of pulls can now reach.",
  "Total live doors": "Every live door you are marketing to after pulling this rung and everything above it, each home counted once.",
  "Which tabs you get": "One tab per section the page is showing for this county, in the same order. Sections the page hides for this county are not exported, so the file and the screen always carry the same set.",
  "Work Order": "The ranking tab for counties the site shows a ladder for. It is a pull order: each rung counts only the deals the rungs above have not already given you, so doors per deal is what that pull costs you NEXT, not what the list is worth on its own.",
  "Priority Ranking": "The ranking tab you get instead when a county has no ladder. Every list is scored standalone against the county baseline. The website makes the same swap, so this workbook only ever carries one ranking, the one on screen.",
  "Rating (1-5)": "The ZIP leaderboard's star rating, written as a number. Five stars is the strongest ZIP in this county's own closed deals.",
  "Momentum (x)": "Recent deal pace against this ZIP's own earlier pace. Above 1.5x reads as heating up, at or below 0.75x as cooling.",
  "best odds": "On Price Bands, the value band where a deal takes the fewest doors worked, among bands with enough supply and enough deals to trust.",
  "Non-disclosure states": "Sale prices are not public there, so deal-dollar columns are omitted; doors per deal and lift never use dollars.",
  "Evidence A / B / C": "from this county's own sold deals / cross-market benchmark / single-market anchor (Knox + Blount TN AI measurement)",
  "Verify supply": "The row tripped the verify rule (v2.1 coverage-aware: verify reasons annotate (churn: doors/deal < 5; small: list < 250) without demoting; only judicial notice lists and churn artifacts (doors/deal < 1) force P3. Volume floors: P1 needs >=2% of county deal flow or >=25 deals, P2 >=1% or >=12 deals): demand is real, treat the efficiency as directional until you price the live list.",
  "The window": "Every count here is the rolling six months the site is showing. Deal counts are read fresh, because county recorders keep filing deeds for weeks after a window closes."
